        -:  167:
        -:  168:    /**
        -:  169:     * Draw an arc segment.
        -:  170:     *
        -:  171:     * This method differs from DrawArc() in what happens when fill/stroke are on or off.
        -:  172:     * DrawArc() draws a "pie piece" when fill is turned on, and a thick stroke when fill is off.
        -:  173:     * DrawArcSegment() with fill *on* behaves like DrawArc() with fill *off*.
        -:  174:     * DrawArcSegment() with fill *off* draws the outline of what it would have drawn with fill on.
        -:  175:     *
        -:  176:     * This has meaning only for back ends that can't draw a true arc, and use segments to
        -:  177:     * approximate.
        -:  178:     *
        -:  179:     * TODO: Unify Arc routines
        -:  180:     *
        -:  181:     * @param aCenterPoint  is the center point of the arc.
        -:  182:     * @param aRadius       is the arc radius.
        -:  183:     * @param aStartAngle   is the start angle of the arc.
        -:  184:     * @param aAngle        is the angle of the arc.
        -:  185:     * @param aWidth        is the thickness of the arc (pen size).
        -:  186:     * @param aMaxError     is the max allowed error to create segments to approximate a circle.
        -:  187:     */
        -:  188:    virtual void DrawArcSegment( const VECTOR2D& aCenterPoint, double aRadius,
        -:  189:                                 const EDA_ANGLE& aStartAngle, const EDA_ANGLE& aAngle,
        -:  190:                                 double aWidth, double aMaxError ){};
